.TH COS 3 "2026-05-03" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
cos, cosf, cosl \- cosine function
.SH LIBRARY
Math Library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.B double cos(double x);
.B float cosf(float x);
.B long double cosl(long double x);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B cos()
function computes the cosine of
.IR x ,
where
.I x
is expressed in radians.
.PP
The
.B cosf()
and
.B cosl()
functions are float and long double variants respectively.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the cosine of
.IR x ,
in the range \fB[\-1, +1]\fR.
.PP
If x is NaN, NaN is returned.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute the cosine of an angle expressed in degrees.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#include <math.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int
main(void)
{
    double deg = 60.0;
    double rad = deg * M_PI / 180.0;

    printf("cos(%.1f deg) = %.6f\en", deg, cos(rad));
    return 0;
}
.EE
.RE
.SH STANDARDS
C99, POSIX.1-2001.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sin (3),
.BR tan (3),
.BR trig (3),
.BR math (7)
